ion/0177d7fa534c75ff5d338933823b11f4bb862c84b895fc983e34c9f40afb42c7" "q-116407/selection/0003121a87755edfb5ec05d2d09627de08ed5a2bb58482e0c87eac370f7f3c3a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-116407" :question/id #uuid "91a16361-849f-5bee-aadf-8394f348cca6" :question/math-academy-id "q-116407" :question/problem "Given the polynomial $P(x)=x(x+3)(x-2),$ find the solution of $P(x)<0.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality $P(x)<0,$ we need to find the values of $x$ for which the curve $y=P(x)$ lies below the $x$-axis.\n\nThe roots of the polynomial $P(x)=x(x+3)(x-2)$ are $x=-3,x=0$ and $x=2,$ which are all simple roots.\n\nAlso, $P(x)$ is a cubic polynomial with a positive leading coefficient. So, we can graph the curve as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033945/assets/d87500612fc14636afa38bd01fdc1b90cf7eecd0bfbd546bff7b14d5a5b30fc8.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving $P(x)<0,$ we look for the part of the curve that is below the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $x\\in (-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (0,2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-116407/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64b71f10-5b2b-5cae-a5dc-b9c160484d82"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-116407"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-116439/selection/c292b16e22500dd6f69908b674a44059df2afebaaa307acbfc2d5eeb931ba48e" :answer/id #uuid "7550b62e-23eb-5aa1-a7e0-55271b9683c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (0,2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116439/selection/bf00229e223e44eb20258cc38287d60c51cdcb0aaefb8c636fad11a1c721095f" :answer/id #uuid "56ac85d6-fed4-5d1a-965f-542f9ecf6e1f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116439/selection/2965c82794a710526d11d6b965136c1ade8b070900bcb8cb2e6528c98ca191bb" :answer/id #uuid "c3b1efc4-4d5b-5699-bda0-1f4193c4524c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (-4,2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116439/selection/0f5c927469ac97c167fc6e1f9e0ee5ca617ee8e73a5c77b6d04edc43f8ce404e" :answer/id #uuid "399af956-c54f-5f1e-86b1-64b649a03fe7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-4)\\cup (2,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116439/selection/2e628efe3e31ea2661e89d853d35adcf31d4ef778430835a6b22d237520ca0bf" :answer/id #uuid "05747928-0930-55a5-a2af-3eca94075285" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (-4,0)\\cup (0,2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116439/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d9353a00-cc9b-570e-b83b-36de6f4e0e6e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-116439/selection/0f5c927469ac97c167fc6e1f9e0ee5ca617ee8e73a5c77b6d04edc43f8ce404e" :answer-field/choices ["q-116439/selection/c292b16e22500dd6f69908b674a44059df2afebaaa307acbfc2d5eeb931ba48e" "q-116439/selection/bf00229e223e44eb20258cc38287d60c51cdcb0aaefb8c636fad11a1c721095f" "q-116439/selection/2965c82794a710526d11d6b965136c1ade8b070900bcb8cb2e6528c98ca191bb" "q-116439/selection/0f5c927469ac97c167fc6e1f9e0ee5ca617ee8e73a5c77b6d04edc43f8ce404e" "q-116439/selection/2e628efe3e31ea2661e89d853d35adcf31d4ef778430835a6b22d237520ca0bf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-116439" :question/id #uuid "88ba9665-3920-5271-b647-ee91ba660327" :question/math-academy-id "q-116439" :question/problem "Given $P(x)={x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2},$ solve $P(x)>0.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality $P(x)>0,$ we need to find the values of $x$ for which the curve $y=P(x)$ lies above the $x$-axis.\n\nFirst, we factor the polynomial $P(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x) & ={x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}({x}^{2}+2x-8) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}({x}^{2}-2x+4x-8) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(x(x-2)+4(x-2)) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(x+4)(x-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe roots of the polynomial $P(x)={x}^{4}+3{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}$ are $x=-4,$ $x=0$ and $x=2,$  where\n\n- $x=0$ has multiplicity $2,$ and\n\n- $x=-4$ and $x=2$ are simple roots.\n\nSo, we can graph the curve as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033945/assets/a357caad0365f296f87367ee4ac1000f1ea772d0d27650c8340d475ca742828b.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving $P(x)>0,$ we look for the part of the curve that is above the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $x\\in (-\\infty ,-4)\\cup (2,\\infty ).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-116439/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "48de9cc7-5f86-51e4-a827-796f77381af2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-116439"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
